00:07:25.000 --> 00:08:06.000
vulnerability, certain life events can make it worse or trigger it in the first place or keep it, make it more recurrent. So both are important. Does that ring true for you, Terry? Are there people in your family who have been diagnosed with bipolar disorder in addition to you? No one in my family that I'm aware of was diagnosed with bipolar disorder, which doesn't mean they didn't have it. They just weren't diagnosed because it wasn't paid much attention to previously. But I certainly felt that I had it, even as a very young child, I had a suicide attempt at age seven. So for me, it went way back.

